    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n31928" root="غصن" body-key="g">
    
      4 
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">اغصن الشَّجَرُ</span></b> , (A in art. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">فرش</span>,) inf. n. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">إِغْصَانٌ</span>,
<i>The trees put forth branches.</i> (KL.) ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b2-  And
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">اغصن</span>, and ↓ <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">غصّن</span></b> , said of a bunch of grapes
(<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">عُنْقُود</span>), <i>It was,</i> or <i>became, large</i> (<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">كَبُرَ</span>, thus in
some of the copies of the K, in other copies <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">كَثُرَ</span>,
but the former is the right, TA) <i>in its berries:</i>
(K:) or <i>somewhat large therein.</i> (TA.)

